# {{ project_slug }}

MLflow training → registration → batch scoring pipeline over the Databricks TPCH sample dataset, deployed as a Databricks Asset Bundle with a scheduled 3-task job.

## Prerequisites

- [Databricks CLI](https://docs.databricks.com/dev-tools/cli/install.html) v0.230+, authenticated (`databricks auth login`)
- A Unity Catalog-enabled workspace with access to `samples.tpch`
- Permission to create catalogs in the metastore — the bundle creates catalog `{{ cfg.catalog }}` and schema `{{ cfg.schema }}` (or your overrides) on deploy

## What's here

```
notebooks/
├── train.py       # Trains a model, logs runs + metrics to the MLflow experiment
├── register.py    # Promotes the best run to the UC Model Registry (see below)
└── score.py       # Batch-scores using the `@champion` alias
resources/jobs/mlflow_job.yml   # 3-task job: train → register → score, scheduled daily at 06:00 UTC
```

### Champion promotion gate

`register.py` only moves the `champion` alias to a new model version if its RMSE beats the
current champion's (or no champion exists yet). A worse run exits early without promoting,
so scheduled retraining can never regress the model that `score.py` uses in production.

## Deploy

```bash
databricks bundle validate --target dev
databricks bundle deploy --target dev
databricks bundle run {{ project_slug | replace("-", "_") }}_pipeline --target dev
```

## Variables

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `catalog` | `{{ cfg.catalog }}` | Catalog for the UC Model Registry and scored output table |
| `schema` | `{{ cfg.schema }}` | Schema for the UC Model Registry and scored output table |
| `experiment_name` | `{{ cfg.experiment_name }}` | MLflow experiment path for training runs |
| `model_name` | `{{ cfg.model_name }}` | Registered model name (`catalog.schema.model_name`) |

## Troubleshooting

- **"Metastore storage root URL does not exist"** — your metastore doesn't have default storage configured, so the bundle can't create `{{ cfg.catalog }}` automatically. Either enable default storage for the metastore (account console → Unity Catalog), or create one catalog manually via the UI first to provision the storage root, then redeploy.
- **`register` exits with "not_promoted"** — expected behavior when the new run doesn't beat the current champion; check the job's task output for the RMSE comparison.
- **`score` fails with "no champion alias"** — run the job at least once end-to-end so `register` sets the initial champion.
